---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import ThemeIcon from "../components/ThemeIcon.astro";
import {Image} from "astro:assets";
---

<Layout title="Portfolio | Lysander Schmidt" ogImage="/header-image.webp">
  <main class="p-8 max-w-screen-sm mx-auto">
    <!-- <img
      data-src="/header-image.webp"
      alt="Header"
      style="width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio: 576 / 329.88; border-radius: 5px;"
      loading="lazy"
    /> -->
    <Image
      src="/header-image.webp"
      alt="Header"
      width={576}
      height={330}
      style={{ width: "100%", height: "auto", borderRadius: "5px" }}
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <!-- <script>
      let loadedimg = false;
      window.onload = () => {
        if (!loadedimg) {
          const imgs = document.querySelectorAll("img");
          imgs.forEach((img) => {
            if (img.dataset.src) {
              img.src = img.dataset.src;
            }
          });
          loadedimg = true;
        }
      };
    </script> -->
    <header class="flex justify-between py-4 items-start">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-lg font-semibold">Lysander Schmidt</h1>
        <p class="text-md text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          <span style="white-space:nowrap;">Autonomous Vehicles </span>
          <span style="white-space:nowrap;">Software Engineer</span>
          <br /><br />
          University of Virginia, 2026<br />
          <span style="white-space:nowrap;">School of Engineering, </span>
          <span style="white-space:nowrap;">B.S. in Computer Science</span>
          <br />
          <span style="white-space:nowrap;">McIntire School of Commerce, </span>
          <span style="white-space:nowrap;">Minor in Leadership</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="flex gap-3 items-center justify-end text-sm text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"
      >
        <a href="/LysanderSchmidtResume.pdf" target="_blank"> Résumé </a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lysanderschmidt/" target="_blank">
          LinkedIn
        </a>
        <ThemeIcon />
      </div>
    </header>
    <section id="projects" class="pt-6">
      <h1 class="font-mono text-lg font-light tracking-tighter">
        Portfolio (WIP)
      </h1><br />
      <ul role="list" class="space-y-4 py-4 text-sm">
        <!-- <Card
          href="https://rightoption.ai"
          title="R⌥AI"
          body="soo helpful"
        /> -->
        <Card badge="Team Member">
          <div slot="title">
            <a
              class="underline underline-offset-4"
              href="https://autonomousracing.dev/"
              target="_blank">Cavalier Racing</a
            > — <a
              class="underline underline-offset-4"
              href="https://www.indyautonomouschallenge.com/"
              target="_blank">Indy Autonomous Challenge</a
            >
          </div>
          Recently, I wrote code to process LiDAR point clouds of racetracks, to
          extract surface normals from the roadway surface. (This was neccessary
          to race at Laguna Seca (first road course), pictured.) Then I extract the
          norms along planned race-lines, and to load them into a k-d tree, which
          serves pitch and roll in real time on the car. This allows the gravity
          component to be accurately subtracted from accelerometer readings, providing
          better inputs to the localization EKF.<br /><br />
          I also recently wrote code to live-compare the expected/optimal with actual
          time for each turn, to help identify which areas to investigate after the
          run.
          <br /><br />
          Current Project: The problem is that the vehicle follows a pre-computed
          race-line, and we modify speed during testing by scaling or setting a maximum
          speed. However, we want to test by setting maximum (lateral and longitudinal)
          tire forces. My project is to compute optimal trajectories and velocity
          profiles constrained by tire-force limitations, on demand.
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <div slot="title">Qwen Attention Visualizer</div>
          I published a <a
            class="underline underline-offset-3"
            target="_blank"
            href="https://storage.googleapis.com/lvs-usa/attention-viz/export_attention_tensors.ipynb"
            >notebook</a
          > to generate tensor files that contain the attention paid by every token
          to every other at every layer in small dense Qwen3 models, and an <a
            class="underline underline-offset-3"
            target="_blank"
            href="https://storage.googleapis.com/lvs-usa/attention-viz/visualizer.html"
            >interactive visualizer</a
          > to explore them. This is useful for understanding how these large language
          models work internally.
          <img
            data-src="/attention_viz_example.webp"
            alt="Header"
            style="width:80%;height:auto;margin:auto;aspect-ratio: 2024/1572; border-radius: 5px;"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          I also published several example tensor files to play with in the visualizer.
          <center class="text-blue-500 dark:text-blue-400">
            <ul>
              <li>
                <a
                  target="_blank"
                  href="https://storage.googleapis.com/lvs-usa/attention-viz/GQA_tensor.bin"
                  >Small (400KB, 4B Model)</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <a
                  target="_blank"
                  href="https://storage.googleapis.com/lvs-usa/attention-viz/dragon_attention_tensor.bin"
                  >Medium (5 MB, 0.6B Model)</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <a
                  target="_blank"
                  href="https://storage.googleapis.com/lvs-usa/attention-viz/vending_machine_attention_tensor.bin"
                  >Large (20MB, 4B Model)</a
                >
              </li>
            </ul>
          </center>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <div slot="title">
            <a
              class="underline underline-offset-4"
              href="https://banana-scanner.lvas.dev/"
              target="_blank">Banana Scanner</a
            >
          </div>
          One of my friends is colorblind in a way that makes it hard to tell green
          bananas from yellow ones. I built a tool to highlight green on bananas
          so he can know differentiate them. It’s been optimized for (his) iPhone
          camera/lighting, but should work on other devices too. Feel free to play
          with it yourself. <br /><br />
          <img
            data-src="/scanned_banana.avif"
            alt="Scanned Banana"
            style="width:80%;height:auto;margin:auto;aspect-ratio: 2024/1572; border-radius: 5px;"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </Card>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
